\n\nAlso applies to: 62-63","id":"bc605c99bf3018fedf5d8326dfbe996e5813a35ed236e97750223b5a79a7ce09","intervals":[[49,51]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_host_config_prepare.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Require unit verification before installation."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"14f81e90c4eaade4b5f09611d6af0f99f5dda81c","body":"**Assert heartbeat bytes survive the post-tick rollback test.**\n\nThe fixture at line 561 writes a heartbeat that contains only `at`. The completion-heartbeat reader requires a `root` matching the checkout and a `last_tick` value (`ops/deploy-controller.py:798-810`). This test stubs health, so the reader does not run and the fixture is never checked against it. As written, the fixture does not represent a heartbeat that a completed tick produces. The final assertions at lines 571-572 check only `state/queue.json`. The controller treats the completion heartbeat as byte-identical and never restored (`ops/deploy-controller.py:19`). A rollback that rewrote the heartbeat would still pass this test.\n\nWrite the fixture heartbeat with the producer's `root` and `last_tick` fields. Keep the second-observation failure as the stubbed health result. After `run.run()`, assert that the heartbeat file bytes match the bytes written during the completed tick. Add this check beside the existing queue-bytes assertion.","id":"4582d0682505599230d9102a3f1a6ee119f2d9ab7edd8c7c6f3b3adfb7431df6","intervals":[[561,561]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_runbook.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Assert heartbeat bytes survive the post-tick rollback test."}],"head":"5895df12500ee3b6479eb263f79fc14a80743969","head_tree":"46873591f734edd9075598e36cb2f7298c8b4605","input_scope":[{"blob":"02e30be5d60a4ad11e1dd36faea161155d30c21c","intervals":[[1,81]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_runtime_admission.py"},{"blob":"baf6342c4a4faa3d3d978730fe3c4ad518b30928","intervals":[[1,221]],"path":